From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Run again an access whose host page another thread
 opened.

With host pages larger than Windows pages, an access to a page that
allows it faults when another page in its host page is protected. When
another thread changes a protection in that host page before the fault
is handled, so that the host page allows the access by the time the
handler looks, the access was raised to the program as an access
violation, unless the host page had been kept whole (patch 0986). A
program that protects and unprotects one page while its threads use the
pages beside it saw access violations on memory it can read and write.

The access now runs again whenever the host page allows it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index 4bd4342..f2cef72 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -5469,8 +5469,9 @@ NTSTATUS virtual_handle_fault( struct thread_data *data, EXCEPTION_RECORD *rec,
             ;
         else if (get_host_page_unix_prot( page, NULL, NULL, 0, 0 ) & need)
         {
-            /* another thread kept the host page whole while this access faulted */
-            if (subpage_whole( page )) ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
+            /* Another thread changed a protection in the host page, or kept it whole, while
+             * this access faulted: the host page allows the access now, so it runs again. */
+            ret = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         }
         else if (subpage_hot( page, err == EXCEPTION_WRITE_FAULT, &protected_page ))
         {
-- 
